%I A399818 #6 Sep 17 2026 22:36:34
%S A399818 1,1,1,0,1,1,3,3,17,116,1350,29170
%N A399818 Number of nonequivalent neighborhood-Hausdorff graphs on n vertices.
%C A399818 A graph G is neighborhood-Hausdorff if, for every two distinct vertices x,y, there exist vertices u,v such that x is in N(u), y is in N(v), and N(u) intersect N(v) is empty.
%C A399818 Two such graphs are considered equivalent if their families of open neighborhoods are isomorphic as hypergraphs.
%e A399818 a(5)=1 since C_5 is the unique neighborhood-Hausdorff graph on 5 vertices up to equivalence.
%e A399818 a(8)=17, although there are 19 neighborhood-Hausdorff graphs on 8 vertices up to graph isomorphism, since two pairs have isomorphic families of open neighborhoods.
%Y A399818 Cf. A399817 (labeled neighborhood-Hausdorff graphs), A398780 (nonequivalent neighborhood-Sperner graphs), A399822 (labeled neighborhood-Sperner graphs), A399195 (nonequivalent neighborhood-anti-Sperner graphs).
%K A399818 nonn,more,new
